<title>SRI LANKA: Airlanka pilots threaten to strike - paper.</title>
<headline>Airlanka pilots threaten to strike - paper.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pilots at Sri Lanka's national carrier, Airlanka, are threatening to strike over management plans to upgrade Indian first officers on its Airbus A320 aircraft, the independent Sunday Times said.</p>
<p>The Pilots' Guild is opposed to the move because it impedes the promotions of local pilots, the paper said.</p>
<p>The airline contends that the move was prompted by a shortage of A320 pilots, it said.</p>
<p>Airline officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>Airlanka is to be privatised under a government programme to restructure or privatise loss-making and badly run public enterprises.</p>
</text>
